{
  "note": "Corrections to the OBDb Toyota-Corolla-Hybrid signalset found on the owner's 2019 car; record the log file that proves each change. 7D2 22 1061 (shift position): found by the discovery watch in session-20261113-181624 (app 0.2.1), P R N D B D N R P each held 14-19 s, both bytes matched the lever in every segment (docs/02 section C3). Same request and P/R/N/D codes as VENZAHYBRID_SHIFT in the OBDb Toyota-Venza-Hybrid signalset; B = 8 is from our log. 7D2 22 1076 (READY): signal definition from VENZAHYBRID_READY in the OBDb Toyota-Venza-Hybrid signalset (see ATTRIBUTION.md); the owner's car answered 0F 03 / 0F 0B (bit set) in READY in session-20261113-174656 and -181624; confirmed 2019 in session-20261114-101039: 0F 02 (bit clear) with the ignition ON not READY (12 V 11.5 V) and at switch-off, 0F 03 / 0F 07 in READY; some switch-offs end with NO DATA instead (session-20261114-161118, -180641), see docs/02 C3. Copied unchanged except the id prefix from the same Venza signalset, after the owner's car answered them in the discovery scan (session-20261113-174656, docs/02 C4): 7D2 22 1FA6 odometer (matches 7D2 22 0103), 7D2 22 15E8 12 V statistics, 7D2 22 15E5 12 V capacity, 7D2 22 1060 accelerator, 747 22 1F5B battery-ECU SOC. From the OBDb Toyota-Prius signalset (see ATTRIBUTION.md), after the car answered them in the same scan (docs/02 C5): 747 22 1802 battery fan (unchanged) and 747 22 180B intake air temperature 1, converted exactly from the Prius formula in degrees F (x458/65535 -58) to degrees C (x2290/589815 -50); the Prius IAT 2 signal is left out because this car sends only 2 data bytes. Polling only, no decoding change: 01 5C (oil temperature) every 5 s instead of 1 s, since it is now polled on every design for the warm-up advice and changes slowly. Engine electric water pump, 700 22 1043 (target byte 0 / actual byte 1, x25 rpm) and 700 22 2827 (actual, x40 rpm): from the OBDb Toyota-Prius signalset (see ATTRIBUTION.md), unchanged except the id prefix, copied from HybridLogger profile 9; confirmed on the owner's car in HybridLogger session-20261114-101039 (0 with the engine stopped, 1525-2775 rpm running, 2827 equals byte 1 of 1043; docs/02 C8). Read only while the Advanced screen or a tile shows them. The inverter water pump duty 7D2 22 1112 is refused on this car (NRC 31). Polling only: 7D2 22 10B2 (inverter coolant) every 5 s instead of 1 s, since the cooling alarms read it all the time (app 0.10.0) and it changes slowly; the engine water pump 700 22 1043 is read every 2 s by the alarms too. Inverter water pump speed, 7D2 22 1039 bytes 2-3, x1 rpm (profile 9, app 0.11.0): copied from HybridLogger profile 15 (docs/02 C13 there). HybridLogger's logs hold 3432 and 3450 rpm parked in READY (session-20261114-180641), about 4250 rpm with the inverter coolant below about 15 C, 160 rpm before READY. Confirmed 2019. The OBDb signal on the same request, COROLLAHYBRID_FRONT_REAR_MOTOR_TQ (an AWD torque ratio; this car is FWD), is disabled. Bytes 0-1 are kept as COROLLAHYBRID_INV_WP_DUTY_1039 with the 1112 duty formula, untested 2019 (not shown). Polled every 2 s, like the engine pump, since the alarms read it all the time. Engine oil temperature (HybridGuard 2026-11-23): 01 5C and the leads 700 22 1F5C / 107B gave no value in two drive logs; the owner chose to drop oil and use the coolant, so derived.json maps oilTemp to nothing (no oil request is sent) and the two leads were removed again. Profile 11 (Battery tab), copied from the HybridMaster profile with the same evidence: 747 22 1807 charge / discharge power limits (-28.1 / +14.8 kW parked, cold, low SOC, session-20261113-174656), 747 22 2802 battery fan level (answered 00 with the engine stopped, session-20261114-010856; untested running), 747 22 181A battery pack 1 / 2 average voltage (3.548 / 3.556 V in session-20261113-174656, where the mean of cells 1-28 / 29-56 read 0.7 s apart was 3.551 / 3.555 V: confirmed 2019) and 747 22 182F cell internal resistance, cells 1-56 (3.6-4.1 milliohms in the same log; formula untested 2019). These four are read only while the Battery tab is open.",
